WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.818
The Tang Monk trembled with fear.

2
00:00:03.819 --> 00:00:06.036
[g@The angry voice spoke again.

3
00:00:06.037 --> 00:00:09.452
"Who is walking on my mountain?"@g]

4
00:00:09.453 --> 00:00:12.001
"Ahh!" cried the Tang Monk.

5
00:00:12.002 --> 00:00:19.162
He fell off his horse and tumbled down the mountain.

6
00:00:19.163 --> 00:00:24.076
At the bottom he saw a crack between the rocks.

7
00:00:24.077 --> 00:00:30.523
The monk looked in and saw a moss-covered monkey peering out at him.

8
00:00:30.524 --> 00:00:33.932
"My name is Sun Wukong," said the monkey.

9
00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:37.648
"I am king of the Fruit and Flower Mountain."

10
00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:40.641
[g@"Why are you in there?" asked the Tang Monk.

11
00:00:40.642 --> 00:00:42.967
He stood up.@g]

12
00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:45.774
"Buddha put me here," said Wukong.

13
00:00:45.775 --> 00:00:48.886
[g@"I am being punished for causing trouble in Heaven.

14
00:00:48.887 --> 00:00:50.676
Who are you?"@g]

15
00:00:50.677 --> 00:00:53.741
"I'm just a monk," said the Tang Monk.

16
00:00:53.742 --> 00:00:57.681
"I'm going to the Western Paradise to get scriptures from Buddha."

17
00:00:57.682 --> 00:01:02.439
Wukong gasped. "You're the Tang Monk!" he cried.

18
00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.271
"I'm supposed to go with you!"

19
00:01:05.272 --> 00:01:08.338
[g@The Tang Monk took a step back.

20
00:01:08.339 --> 00:01:12.239
Was this strange monkey telling the truth?@g]

21
00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.610
"The bodhisattva Guanyin visited me," Wukong went on.

22
00:01:16.611 --> 00:01:20.944
"She said I'd be set free if I promise to protect you on the journey.

23
00:01:20.945 --> 00:01:24.223
Set me free, and I'll go with you to the West."

24
00:01:24.224 --> 00:01:26.934
[g@The Tang Monk relaxed.

25
00:01:26.935 --> 00:01:28.991
He looked at the rocks.@g]

26
00:01:28.992 --> 00:01:30.887
"How can I free you?"

27
00:01:30.888 --> 00:01:35.275
"There's a small piece of paper on top of this mountain," said Wukong.

28
00:01:35.276 --> 00:01:41.282
"You must remove it."

29
00:01:41.283 --> 00:01:44.538
The Tang Monk went back up the mountain.

30
00:01:44.539 --> 00:01:55.638
He pushed aside shrubs and brambles and pulled himself over large boulders.

31
00:01:55.639 --> 00:02:04.314
Finally he reached the mountain's peak.

32
00:02:04.315 --> 00:02:06.841
[g@The monk picked up the paper.

33
00:02:06.842 --> 00:02:11.102
Right away a breeze swept it from his hand.@g]

34
00:02:11.103 --> 00:02:15.870
The paper floated up and then disappeared among the clouds.

35
00:02:15.871 --> 00:02:20.401
The monk hurried back down the mountain.

36
00:02:20.402 --> 00:02:24.306
"The paper floated away," he said to the monkey.

37
00:02:24.307 --> 00:02:26.976
[g@"It returned to Buddha," said Wukong.

38
00:02:26.977 --> 00:02:28.654
"Now step back."@g]

39
00:02:28.655 --> 00:02:32.806
The Tang Monk took a step back.

40
00:02:32.807 --> 00:02:35.685
"Go farther," said Wukong.

41
00:02:35.686 --> 00:02:38.387
The monk took another step back.

42
00:02:38.388 --> 00:02:43.685
"Go farther," said Wukong again.

43
00:02:43.686 --> 00:02:47.709
The Tang Monk went far from the mountain.

44
00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:52.744
He gasped as the entire mountain rose into the air.

45
00:02:52.745 --> 00:02:58.353
Wukong stood under the mountain, holding it up with his hands.

46
00:02:58.354 --> 00:03:06.241
He jumped out, and the mountain crashed down behind him.

47
00:03:06.242 --> 00:03:09.498
Wukong grabbed the Tang Monk's hands.

48
00:03:09.499 --> 00:03:14.865
"Thank you, Master! I will help you reach the Western Paradise."

49
00:03:14.866 --> 00:03:18.626
The Tang Monk rode the horse as Wukong walked.

50
00:03:18.627 --> 00:03:21.384
The monkey told the monk about himself.

51
00:03:21.385 --> 00:03:26.996
"The Jade Emperor's entire army couldn't defeat me." He laughed.

52
00:03:26.997 --> 00:03:30.298
"So I said [i@I@i] should be in charge of Heaven."

53
00:03:30.299 --> 00:03:33.979
"What powers do you have?" asked the Tang Monk.

54
00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:40.328
"I can become other animals," said Wukong. "Watch this!"

55
00:03:40.329 --> 00:03:43.062
[g@He quickly changed into a tiger.

56
00:03:43.063 --> 00:03:45.138
The Tang Monk gulped.@g]

57
00:03:45.139 --> 00:03:50.693
Wukong changed into a snake, a vulture, and then back into himself.

58
00:03:50.694 --> 00:03:52.833
[g@"And that's not all," he said.

59
00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:57.089
"I can grow big!"@g]

60
00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:02.176
The monkey's body grew so big that his head reached the clouds.

61
00:04:02.177 --> 00:04:05.872
"And I can become tiny!" said Wukong.

62
00:04:05.873 --> 00:04:10.551
He shrank to the size of a bee and hopped onto the monk's head.

63
00:04:10.552 --> 00:04:14.012
[g@"I can do more!" said Wukong.

64
00:04:14.013 --> 00:04:17.285
He changed back to his normal size.@g]

65
00:04:17.286 --> 00:04:22.272
His iron bar appeared from his ear.

66
00:04:22.273 --> 00:04:27.045
The monkey spun it around and then struck a huge boulder.

67
00:04:27.046 --> 00:04:32.806
[i@Smash!@i] The boulder exploded into tiny pieces.

68
00:04:32.807 --> 00:04:36.034
The Tang Monk watched in horror.

69
00:04:36.035 --> 00:04:40.303
[g@Wukong laughed. "Don't look so scared, Master.

70
00:04:40.304 --> 00:04:43.315
I'm protecting you!"@g]

71
00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:48.597
The two traveled farther until they saw a group of men blocking the road.

72
00:04:48.598 --> 00:04:50.756
[g@The men looked rough and mean.

73
00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:53.454
They all had weapons.@g]

74
00:04:53.455 --> 00:04:57.483
One man stepped forward and waved a sword.

75
00:04:57.484 --> 00:05:05.842
"Give us your money, or you'll be sorry!"

